{"id": "1.2-00045", "case_id": "opencores_sha256_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "opencores/crypto_core_sha_cores", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (6 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: rtl/sha256.v. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>1 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Frtl%2Fsha256.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed verification testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>4 verification testpoints:</strong> short_messages, padding_boundaries, multiple_blocks, reset_restart. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># Implement the SHA-256 core project configuration\nRead the original SHA core project manual. Implement the complete SHA-256\nconfiguration in rtl/sha256.v with module sha256. SHA-1/SHA-512 are other project\nconfigurations and are not required. This project configuration has one RTL module.\n\nProtocol clarifications:\n- Active-high synchronous reset. Input/output words are 32 bits, big-endian\n  within the message/digest. The host supplies SHA-256 padded 512-bit blocks,\n  including the 0x80 padding and final 64-bit big-endian message bit length.\n  Padding is performed by the host, not by this core.\n- Pulse cmd_w_i for one rising edge to write cmd_i. Command 010 starts a FIRST\n  block using standard SHA-256 IV; 110 continues from the prior block state.\n  Starting on the following rising edge, supply 16 consecutive text_i words,\n  most significant word first. No separate per-word valid or backpressure exists.\n  Run all 64 SHA-256 rounds and add the previous chaining state.\n- cmd_o[3] is registered busy; [2] is first/continuation selection and [1:0]\n  are command write/read bits. Hardware clears [1:0] when idle. Busy becomes\n  visible shortly after command acceptance and clears after block completion;\n  complete within 128 clocks of accepting the sixteenth input word. Do not\n  issue another command while busy. First-block commands restart the digest\n  without requiring hardware reset; reset can abort an in-progress operation.\n- After completion pulse command 001 to read. Let C be the edge accepting that\n  command: C+1 initializes the read pointer; C+2 through C+9 output the eight\n  digest words in H0..H7 order. The last word holds while idle. Re-reading a\n  completed digest is permitted. text_o while hashing is not a valid digest.\n\nPrivate equal-weight points check short messages, padding boundaries, multiple\nblocks, and reset/restart sequences against an independent SHA-256 library.\nNo internal RTL, intermediate trace, or private testbench is supplied to the agent.\n\nImplement every required path in output_contract.json. Declaration-only ports\nare in interfaces/modules.v. No initial/final, delays, simulation system tasks,\nforce/release or external includes are permitted. Only declared RTL is collected.\nMissing files, forbidden constructs or failed top compilation score zero. Each\nprivate point has equal weight and requires all of its checks to pass. Use\nterminal/file_editor, iverilog, vvp and Python iteratively; finish by saving RTL.\nRun `python3 checks/check.py` for public compilation feedback.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/a2f43b35a2b1fd8dee4bbac719ebdbebf1f773a3a9f2aae4fa3e1200b86d2606.txt", "size": 30223, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/771e58998dfa59d19bd4591ce49673fcbadd56239829b74d2a9c5869aef77295.txt", "size": 4693, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/sha256.v", "url": "assets/1e7d1e5bc962f56f9225e8284a3da4183c25d9c6193edf8fa934dac7a4b300b9.txt", "size": 33632, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/choose_function/multiple_blocks/compile.command.json", "url": "assets/659fbb27225cc662b1bbacafafeb72447edc976ea513cb7a9a1edb890486ccfc.txt", "size": 2062, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/choose_function/multiple_blocks/compile.result.json", "url": "assets/1e3f6691f455051e8adb15d961e4bf3c7a17e83dd88b2afdd13315cc288250bb.txt", "size": 22, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/choose_function/multiple_blocks/simulate.command.json", "url": "assets/d327537b5955eff45214be71d88e2e5d71ffbe74f65e96a2d805aa0c1cb0edf3.txt", "size": 1961, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/choose_function/multiple_blocks/simulate.result.json", "url": "assets/b9f87d4ceb14f54a8787da14c5985aa499e13197fe39c8f0f4ecf87e7a01957e.txt", "size": 22, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/choose_function/padding_boundaries/compile.command.json",