nary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/verification/multiple_blocks.v", "url": "assets/af8299a9947eb105bf8113ddd56197151634e1ff55ccf77db0bfb8cce7facc01.txt", "size": 32498, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/verification/padding_boundaries.v", "url": "assets/c52202d4d0c48b8edd40c4489132529d5e2ef50ce070533cb42eac1acbb45f37.txt", "size": 14093, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/verification/reset_restart.v", "url": "assets/aadcbdfc743e6b44694d16f4d1e765337b0509625c1033c07ad3661c25901815.txt", "size": 10163, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/verification/short_messages.v", "url": "assets/83076dd293f68f5290e2262d068f9da240eb809830e34a6ed67b9d7f16b86fc4.txt", "size": 12136, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "public/checks/check.py", "url": "assets/4b3c0627c5410d2a9c4cbc55674d36c5412182f794cb162680db66f457305ccf.txt", "size": 390, "binary": false, "section": "Public / stage input: public"}, {"name": "public/instruction.md", "url": "assets/b022411005b33cb0345b657b96e0c827a549e5b803b4c8145bcc38e7bdcf1f17.txt", "size": 2534, "binary": false, "section": "Public / stage input: public"}, {"name": "public/interfaces/modules.v", "url": "assets/05177b65f72809f6e5bc57b12fc26bd7fd17d817f43e943515f700046b4fd335.txt", "size": 275, "binary": false, "section": "Public / stage input: public"}, {"name": "public/output_contract.json", "url": "assets/894dcf96fd0f967437229809458795ad7b192724a78e4b07ca19f558956214f7.txt", "size": 168, "binary": false, "section": "Public / stage input: public"}, {"name": "public/specification/project.pdf", "url": "assets/cddf4f88c525e9be6c73fbed47ffed062a11398ca8d6ddbd9652b659434fc0a4.pdf", "size": 44263, "binary": true, "section": "Public / stage input: public"}, {"name": "public/specification/project.txt", "url": "assets/71e98858889aa48e7dc7b2fce31435c76148a29aa591a93a071c79bcb8bdc676.txt", "size": 2027, "binary": false, "section": "Public / stage input: public"}], "entry_point": "<h2>Agent entry point — start here</h2><div class='card entry-point'><table><tbody><tr><th>Starting instruction</th><td><strong><a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>instruction.md</a></strong> → <code>/workspace/instruction.md</code> in the agent workspace.</td></tr><tr><th>Available context</th><td>The launcher copies this case’s <code>public/</code> contents into an isolated workspace, without the <code>public/</code> prefix. Reference RTL and private verification assets are outside that workspace.</td></tr><tr><th>How files are read</th><td>The launch message directs the agent to read the instruction, specifications, interfaces, and output contract. The harness supplies file-reading, shell, and editing tools. The agent chooses tool calls; these supporting files are not automatically concatenated into the initial message.</td></tr><tr><th>Required submission</th><td>Implement every RTL path in <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>output_contract.json</a>. Save the files in the workspace; a final chat response alone is not the RTL submission.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Initial agent message: recorded Codex example</h3><p class='muted small'>Recorded GPT-5.6 Sol / Codex campaign template; this is not evidence that this case was run. Other harnesses can use different framing: the OpenHands launcher passes the case instruction as the initial message through <code>TASK.md</code>.</p><pre>Implement the RTL project described in /workspace/instruction.md.\nRead its specification, interfaces and output_contract.json, then create every\nrequired RTL file at its declared path. You may use the installed tools to write\nyour own tests, compile, simulate and revise your implementation. Run the public\nchecks before finishing. Only the declared RTL files will be submitted for final\nevaluation. You have up to 30 minutes for this attempt; no hidden test feedback\nis available. Save your implementation in the workspace and finish with a brief\ndescription of what you implemented and tested.</pre><h3>Input files to follow</h3><ol><li>Read the starting instruction: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>instruction.md</a></li><li>Check the required output paths and top module: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>output_contract.json</a></li><li>Read the project specifications: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Fspecification%2Fproject.pdf'>specification/project.pdf</a> · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Fspecification%2Fproject.txt'>specification/project.txt</a></li><li>Read the declaration-only interfaces: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Finterfaces%2Fmodules.v'>interfaces/modules.v</a></li><li>Inspect available public checks: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00045&amp;file=public%2Fchecks%2Fcheck.py'>checks/check.py</a></li></ol><p class='muted small'>This is a navigation guide, not a claim that the agent read every file. Audit the actual run’s <code>prompt.txt</code>, <code>visible_inputs.json</code>, and <code>events.jsonl</code> for its starting message, available inputs, and file-reading/tool calls. Raw experiment logs are not included in the public case browser.</p></div>"}
